# Hostinger deploy zip

When the user asks for a deploy zip, produce `blinkfinance-public_html.zip` as a **flat `public_html` dump** (zip root = site root). Never wrap files in `dist/`, `build/`, or a named folder.

## Canonical `public_html` layout (do not invent a different tree)

```
public_html/
  api/            ← server-only; never delete; do not put in the React zip
  lms/            ← server-only; never delete; do not put in the React zip
  assets/
  banks/
  clients/
  directors/
  fonts/
  loans/
  .htaccess
  apply.html      ← server-only; leave on host
  contact.html    ← server-only; leave on host
  insurance.html  ← server-only; leave on host
  enquiry.php     ← server-only; leave on host
  send.php        ← server-only; leave on host
  index.html
  favicon.png
  icons.svg
  new_logo.png
  robots.txt
  sitemap.xml
  Scene.json
  business_bg_3d.jpg
  main_office_3d.jpg
  ChatGPT_Image_Aug_16__2026__11_53_29_PM-removebg-preview.png
```

## How to build the zip

1. `npm run build`
2. Zip **contents of `dist/`** (including `.htaccess`), not the `dist` folder itself.
3. Extract instructions: inside `public_html`, overwrite, then delete the zip on the server.

## Extra files

If the build adds a file/folder **not** in the layout above, still include it in the zip if the site needs it, and **tell the user by name** what is new, why it is needed, and that they should overwrite/extract it. Do not silently change the expected tree.
